=== Projection to the original N=10/100/1,000 benchmark batches (Section
=== "Scalability and Performance", Table tab:benchmark) ===
=== Because the reconstruction above is confirmed byte-for-byte identical
=== to a live-captured event, the same JSON-encoding method (Go's
=== encoding/json, alphabetically sorted map keys, no inserted whitespace)
=== was applied to the real token IDs and real recall transaction IDs
=== already committed for the N=10/100/1,000 benchmark batches
=== (BCOMP-10-1..10, BCOMP-100-1..100, BCOMP-1000B-1..1000; real txIds
=== taken from evidence/benchmark_N*_recall_output.log), rather than
=== re-triggering those already-recalled batches (a repeat TriggerRecall
=== on an already-recalled batch returns affectedCount:0 with an empty
=== recalledTokens array, which would not reproduce the original event).

N=10  (batch BENCH-10,    txId 599154021ebfac90b36620157972962a97bae138085744b4dc669cb17c8a7dae): 320 bytes
N=100 (batch BENCH-100,   txId bbc26235d4a06e9c5e0e79e5af036612a70e65d3317c159401a5489518f4ecb8): 1,683 bytes
